@startuml sample_rate_range
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam ArrowFontColor #e6edf7
title Which sample rates all three parts accept on this carrier (axis in kHz, cut at 60 kHz)
robust "INMP441 microphone\nWS frequency (datasheet Table 3)" as microphone
robust "PCM5102A, SCK to ground, PLL from BCK\nBCK = 64 fS (datasheet Table 11)" as dac
robust "ESP32-S3 I2S, 160 MHz source\nproject calculation (TRM 28.6, driver)" as controller
microphone has accepted,outside
dac has listed,unlisted
controller has reachable,outside
scale 4 as 50 pixels
@0
microphone is outside
dac is unlisted
controller is outside
@2.44
controller is reachable
@7.8
microphone is accepted
@15.6
dac is listed
@16.4
dac is unlisted
@31.6
dac is listed
@32.4
dac is unlisted
@43.7
dac is listed
@44.5
dac is unlisted
@47.6
dac is listed
@48.4
dac is unlisted
@50
microphone is outside
@60
highlight 15.8 to 16.2 #52c7b4 : 16 kHz chosen
legend bottom
  Microphone: 7.8 to 50 kHz. DAC: Table 11 lists 16, 32, 44.1 and 48 kHz (and 96, 192, 384 kHz) for BCK = 64 fS, and no entry at 8 kHz;
  rates between the listed ones are not stated. Controller: fS = 160 MHz ÷ (256 × N) with the integer divider N = 2…256, so about 2.44 to 312.5 kHz;
  the fractional divider is not evaluated, and this range is a project calculation, not a documented limit.
  16 kHz is the lowest rate that all three accept; it carries content up to 8 kHz (sampling theorem); the candidate filter bands end at 800 Hz (P08).
endlegend
@enduml
